      "side": 1,
      "message": "Concurrency Bug Due to Shared State: The variables proc_start_timestampMs and curr_proc_complete_timestampMs appear to be member variables of the distance_measurement_manager. If this manager handles multiple ranging procedures for different Bluetooth connections at the same time, this will not work correctly. One procedure\u0027s start time will be overwritten by another\u0027s, leading to completely wrong duration calculations.\n\nFix: The start timestamp should not be a member of the manager. It must be stored in a structure that is unique to each procedure, such as the procedure_data or live_tracker object.",
