      "side": 1,
      "message": "Incorrect Clock Source: The code uses gettimeofday(), which measures wall-clock time. This clock is not suitable for measuring elapsed time because it\u0027s not monotonic. It can jump forwards or backwards if the user changes the system time or due to network time synchronization (NTP). This can lead to incorrect or even negative durations.\n\nFix: You must use a monotonic clock for measuring durations. The standard modern C++ solution is std::chrono::steady_clock.",
      "revId": "382404c25bbc609d8a9e550da06012b3f8d3e175",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1a5f788f_d490627e",
        "filename": "system/gd/hci/distance_measurement_manager.cc",
