      "side": 1,
      "message": "Magic Numbers and Casting: The code uses magic numbers like 1e6 (a double) and 1000, along with a C-style cast to (long). This can lead to subtle floating-point precision issues and potential data truncation if the duration exceeds the capacity of a long.\n\nFix: Using std::chrono (as suggested above) completely eliminates the need for manual conversions and magic numbers.",
      "revId": "382404c25bbc609d8a9e550da06012b3f8d3e175",
